Subject: win32u: include the non-client area in SetSysColors's forced
 repaint

NtUserSetSysColors already tries to force affected windows to repaint after
a color change (NtUserRedrawWindow with RDW_INVALIDATE|RDW_ERASE|
RDW_UPDATENOW|RDW_ALLCHILDREN), matching real Windows' documented behavior
of refreshing any window displaying an affected color - but RDW_ALLCHILDREN
alone only reaches client areas. RDW_FRAME was missing, so the non-client
area (menu bars, captions) never got included. Confirmed missing in
practice: an external SetSysColors call never repainted a window's native
menu bar at all, requiring a caller to separately enumerate every window
and call DrawMenuBar on each one, entirely outside this function, to get
the same effect this one-flag fix now gives for free to any caller.
---
 dlls/win32u/sysparams.c | 10 ++++++++--
 1 file changed, 8 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/dlls/win32u/sysparams.c b/dlls/win32u/sysparams.c
index bb4f9d71..18cc50c6 100644
--- a/dlls/win32u/sysparams.c
+++ b/dlls/win32u/sysparams.c
@@ -7427,8 +7427,14 @@ BOOL WINAPI NtUserSetSysColors( INT count, const INT *colors, const COLORREF *va
     /* Send WM_SYSCOLORCHANGE message to all windows */
     send_message_timeout( HWND_BROADCAST, WM_SYSCOLORCHANGE, 0, 0,
                           SMTO_ABORTIFHUNG, 2000, FALSE );
-    /* Repaint affected portions of all visible windows */
-    NtUserRedrawWindow( 0, NULL, 0, RDW_INVALIDATE | RDW_ERASE | RDW_UPDATENOW | RDW_ALLCHILDREN );
+    /* Repaint affected portions of all visible windows. RDW_FRAME too: real
+     * Windows' SetSysColors is documented to refresh any window displaying an
+     * affected color, and that includes the non-client area (menu bars,
+     * captions) - RDW_ALLCHILDREN alone only reaches client areas. Confirmed
+     * missing in practice: an external SetSysColors call never repainted a
+     * window's native menu bar at all without a caller separately forcing
+     * DrawMenuBar on every window afterward, entirely outside this function. */
+    NtUserRedrawWindow( 0, NULL, 0, RDW_INVALIDATE | RDW_FRAME | RDW_ERASE | RDW_UPDATENOW | RDW_ALLCHILDREN );
     return TRUE;
 }
 
